<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Svarožič</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Svarozhich, Zuarasici</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Svarožič was a West Slavic god whose temple at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rethra">Rethra</a>, among the Lutici, is described by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thietmar-of-merseburg">Thietmar of Merseburg</a> around 1015 under the name Zuarasici. His name means 'son of Svarog', and he is often linked with fire or the sun. The missionary Bruno of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/querfurt">Querfurt</a> also names him in 1008 as a god of the pagan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavs">Slavs</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/svarozic.jpg" alt="Svarožič" width="320" height="224" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Union of Slavic Rodnover Communities (Союз Славянских Общин Славянской Родной Веры) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kupala_2015_in_Krasotinka,_Kaluga_(5).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
